<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $61.4 mln Oct 22.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $61.4 mln Oct 22.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $61.4 million deficit on October 22 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank</p>
<p>issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 22</p>
<p>Exports: $164.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $225.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $178.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $178.3 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $61.4 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.624 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.717 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.502 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.649 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.760 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
